{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T6JQA5CQo3BF8mRka4GuaV","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex 007e8323..ba61c646 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -258,6 +258,7 @@ pose delegate handoff <run> --to <agent|auto> [--dry-run] [--json]\n pose delegate cancel <run> [--json]\n pose delegate agents [--json]\n pose runtime serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart [--idle <d>] [--drain <d>] [--json]  # optional per-worktree runtime; opt-in, standalone without it\n+pose runtime run [--envelope] [--timeout <d>] <review-check|closeout-check|artifact-check|surface-check|roadmap-check> [args...]  # runs the check in the runtime when there is one, else standalone\n \n # Project state and docs governance\n pose state [init|refresh [--if-stale]|diff]  # native project-state artifact; no subcommand = validate\n@@ -945,7 +946,7 @@ Reservations live in `.pose/review-attempts/`, final receipts link the run, and\n \n **Optional worktree runtime.** `pose runtime start` starts, detached, a runtime for this worktree; `attach` and `status` handshake with it, `stop` drains it (`--drain <d>`, default 5s) and says how many requests in flight finished and how many were abandoned, `restart` is stop then start, and `serve` runs it in the foreground (`--idle <d>`, default 30m, stops an idle runtime; 0 never does). It is opt-in: no other command starts it, and every command runs standalone whether it runs or not. The runtime is identified by the user, the canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) and the Git common directory, so two worktrees of one repository, or two users, never share one; the handshake compares the engine, build, protocol and schema as well and an attach from another engine is refused naming the field. Its endpoint is a Unix domain socket (Linux, macOS) of mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user (`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pose`, else `pose-runtime-<uid>` under the temporary directory, or `POSE_RUNTIME_DIR`), whose peer the operating system identifies before a byte is read; a link, a loose mode, another owner or a file that is not a socket is refused, and a socket nobody answers on is replaced. There is no TCP and no token. Slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers handshake, status and stop, confers no authority, signature or presence, and every restart has a new epoch, inheriting nothing. On Windows, which has no named-pipe implementation here, `status` reports `unsupported` and every command runs standalone. `status` exits 0 for running, standalone and unsupported and 1 for an incompatible runtime; `attach` also exits 1 when there is nothing to attach to. `--json` prints the document `pose.runtime.status/1`.\n \n-**Review rounds.** The rounds of a scope are its sealed bundles that a completed delegated review concluded on, in the order those runs ended; `pose review verify`, `pose delegate ls` and `pose insights` show the round. From round 2, the generated brief (template `review-brief/2`; runs briefed with `review-brief/1` still verify) carries a `Previous round` section built from the ledger: every open finding with the identifier it keeps across rounds (`R<round>-<id>`), its severity, disposition and location, the previous run and its draft digest. The reviewer's draft is the fenced code block whose info string is `pose-draft`: JSON with `schema` `pose.review.draft/v1`, `decision` and `findings` (`id`, `severity` high|medium|low, `disposition` blocker|follow-up, `file`, `line`, `summary`), and from round 2 `prior_findings` (`id`, `status` fixed|partial|not-fixed|superseded, `evidence`) and `sweep`. A finding reported `partial` or `not-fixed` keeps its identifier in the next brief. A round-2-or-later draft that leaves an open finding unaccounted, calls one `fixed` without evidence or states no sweep is recorded with `draft_problems`, `wait` reports it as `invalid`, and it is never accepted as an approval. With `routing.rounds` `continue-thread` (the default) a round resumes the session the previous round ended with, through the agent's resume command; it opens a new session, recording why, when the agent or its vendor changes, the chain of drafts is broken, that session cannot be resumed, or the round reaches `routing.round_threshold` (5 by default), where `verify` also warns that the rounds are not converging. `cold-session` opens a new session every round. Each run records its `round` and `thread`; `pose insights` reports, per scope, findings per round, rounds to approval, and how prior findings were accounted for in continued and in cold rounds. A previous round whose record is not intact makes the brief refuse.\n+**Hosted checks and the resident Git memo.** `pose runtime run [--envelope] [--timeout <d>] <command> [args...]` runs `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check`, `surface-check` or `roadmap-check` in the runtime of the worktree when one is running, compatible and willing, and standalone in this process otherwise; the exit code and the output are the command's, and `--envelope` prints one document (`pose.runtime.run/1`) with them and with `via` (`runtime` or `standalone`), the `fallback_reason`, the typed `outcome` (`completed`; `error` when the command ran and ended but its output (over 2 MiB) is not sent back, with the command's exit code; or `unknown` for a deadline or a lost answer), the epoch and the memo hits. The runtime refuses, before the command starts, one it does not host and a caller whose environment digest (the `POSE_`, `HARNE8_`, `GIT_`, `CLAUDE` and `CODEX` variables, `XDG_STATE_HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, the locale, `HOME`, `NO_COLOR` and the user) differs from its own, so the caller runs standalone; a command that reached the runtime and whose answer did not come back whole, or whose `--timeout` passed, may have run and is never repeated standalone unasked: it exits 1 and says so. The runtime runs one hosted command at a time, and a command still waiting for its turn when its `--timeout` passes is refused, not started, so the caller runs it standalone; as the user that started it, in its worktree, with the output of a non-terminal. A runtime also keeps, between commands, the output of the Git reads that are pure functions of object ids or of the commit HEAD named when they ran, keyed by that commit and the shallow state (256 MiB, least recently used first; not for a linked worktree): the second `review-check` of this repository took about 10 s against about 25 s standalone, with the same output.\\n\\n**Review rounds.** The rounds of a scope are its sealed bundles that a completed delegated review concluded on, in the order those runs ended; `pose review verify`, `pose delegate ls` and `pose insights` show the round. From round 2, the generated brief (template `review-brief/2`; runs briefed with `review-brief/1` still verify) carries a `Previous round` section built from the ledger: every open finding with the identifier it keeps across rounds (`R<round>-<id>`), its severity, disposition and location, the previous run and its draft digest. The reviewer's draft is the fenced code block whose info string is `pose-draft`: JSON with `schema` `pose.review.draft/v1`, `decision` and `findings` (`id`, `severity` high|medium|low, `disposition` blocker|follow-up, `file`, `line`, `summary`), and from round 2 `prior_findings` (`id`, `status` fixed|partial|not-fixed|superseded, `evidence`) and `sweep`. A finding reported `partial` or `not-fixed` keeps its identifier in the next brief. A round-2-or-later draft that leaves an open finding unaccounted, calls one `fixed` without evidence or states no sweep is recorded with `draft_problems`, `wait` reports it as `invalid`, and it is never accepted as an approval. With `routing.rounds` `continue-thread` (the default) a round resumes the session the previous round ended with, through the agent's resume command; it opens a new session, recording why, when the agent or its vendor changes, the chain of drafts is broken, that session cannot be resumed, or the round reaches `routing.round_threshold` (5 by default), where `verify` also warns that the rounds are not converging. `cold-session` opens a new session every round. Each run records its `round` and `thread`; `pose insights` reports, per scope, findings per round, rounds to approval, and how prior findings were accounted for in continued and in cold rounds. A previous round whose record is not intact makes the brief refuse.\n \n **Delegated runs over MCP.** `pose_delegate_start` (review, adjudicate or smoke), `pose_delegate_status`, `pose_delegate_wait`, `pose_delegate_resume` and `pose_delegate_handoff` run `pose delegate … --json` in the project the server resolved for the call, so every plan, refusal and run is the CLI's: a start, resume or handoff is always detached and returns once the run has reserved its attempt (without `apply` it previews), a status never blocks, and a wait blocks at most its `timeout_seconds` (300 at most), returning `still-running` when the bound passes. Refusals carry the same `reason_code` as the CLI's error document (`rerun-without-reason`, `budget-exhausted`, `containment-incompatible`, `agent-unavailable`, `no-agent`), and results carry the normalized summary only: no transcript, prompt, session reference or environment value. `pose delegate resume` and `handoff` take `--detach` as the purposes do. A task is not started over MCP.\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go\nindex 6d4c684c..5bb875d0 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go\n@@ -518,7 +518,7 @@ Governed closeout:\n   review record <scope> [...]         Compatibility entrypoint\n   action <open|list|show|resolve|...> Open, read and resolve material requests to a person or system\n   delegate review <scope> [--agent]   Run a delegated review; also adjudicate, smoke, ls, resume, cancel, agents\n-  runtime <serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart>   Optional per-worktree runtime (opt-in); commands run standalone without it\n+  runtime <serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart|run>   Optional per-worktree runtime (opt-in); run hosts the checks in it; commands run standalone without it\n   close <scope>                         Apply a review-gated lifecycle transition\n   continuous-closeout <action>          Persist and project a terminal scope\n   artifact-backfill --from-git          Propose explicit historical provenance\n@@ -600,7 +600,7 @@ Fechamento governado:\n   review record <escopo> [...]         Entrada de compatibilidade\n   action <open|list|show|resolve|...>  Abre, lê e resolve pedidos materiais a uma pessoa ou sistema\n   delegate review <escopo> [--agent]   Roda um review delegado; também adjudicate, smoke, ls, resume, cancel, agents\n-  runtime <serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart>   Runtime opcional por worktree (opt-in); sem ele os comandos rodam standalone\n+  runtime <serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart|run>   Runtime opcional por worktree (opt-in); run hospeda os checks nele; sem ele os comandos rodam standalone\n   close <escopo>                        Aplica transição de ciclo de vida governada\n   continuous-closeout <ação>            Persiste e projeta um escopo terminal\n   artifact-backfill --from-git          Propõe proveniência histórica explícita\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\nindex c0b7a760..eaa72b65 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\n@@ -11,9 +11,11 @@ import (\n \t\"os/signal\"\n \t\"runtime/debug\"\n \t\"strings\"\n+\t\"sync/atomic\"\n \t\"syscall\"\n \t\"time\"\n \n+\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n \t\"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/version\"\n \t\"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime\"\n )\n@@ -88,10 +90,13 @@ func parseRuntimeFlags(args []string) (runtimeFlags, string) {\n func cmdRuntime(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n \tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n \tif len(args) == 0 {\n-\t\tout.Usage(tr(\"usage: pose runtime <serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart> [--idle <d>] [--drain <d>] [--json]\", \"uso: pose runtime <serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart> [--idle <d>] [--drain <d>] [--json]\"))\n+\t\tout.Usage(tr(\"usage: pose runtime <serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart|run> [--idle <d>] [--drain <d>] [--json]\", \"uso: pose runtime <serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart|run> [--idle <d>] [--drain <d>] [--json]\"))\n \t\treturn 2\n \t}\n \tsub := args[0]\n+\tif sub == \"run\" {\n+\t\treturn cmdRuntimeRun(root, args[1:], stdout, stderr)\n+\t}\n \tf, problem := parseRuntimeFlags(args[1:])\n \tif problem != \"\" {\n \t\tout.Failure(\"pose runtime: \" + problem)\n@@ -111,7 +116,11 @@ func cmdRuntime(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n \t\tserveCtx, cancel := context.WithCancel(ctx)\n \t\tdefer cancel()\n \t\tgo func() { <-sigs; cancel() }()\n-\t\tif err := worktreeruntime.Serve(serveCtx, worktreeruntime.Options{Identity: id, Dir: client.Dir, Idle: f.idle}); err != nil {\n+\t\t// A resident process keeps the pure Git reads it makes between hosted commands.\n+\t\tposemodel.EnableResidentGitMemo(256 << 20)\n+\t\tdefer posemodel.DisableResidentGitMemo()\n+\t\tvar busy atomic.Int64\n+\t\tif err := worktreeruntime.Serve(serveCtx, worktreeruntime.Options{Identity: id, Dir: client.Dir, Idle: f.idle, Busy: busy.Load, Handler: runtimeHostedHandler(runtimeEnvDigest(os.Environ()), &busy)}); err != nil {\n \t\t\treturn runtimeFailure(out, stdout, f, \"serve\", err)\n \t\t}\n \t\treturn 0\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\nindex 7048ceb3..090ed2f5 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n@@ -333,7 +333,28 @@ func (state *governanceReadViewGitState) capture(files Files, ctx context.Contex\n \tif byHead {\n \t\theadBefore = governanceHeadAt(ctx, files, root)\n \t}\n-\tstdout, stderr, runErr := runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmittedContext(ctx, files, root, args, limit, state.op.reserveInput)\n+\t// A process that turned the resident memo on answers a pure read from it; the bytes are\n+\t// admitted against the operation's budget as a fresh read's are.\n+\tvar stdout, stderr []byte\n+\tvar runErr error\n+\tmemoKey, memoized := \"\", false\n+\tmemo := residentGit.Load()\n+\tif memo != nil && (byObject || byHead && headBefore != \"\") {\n+\t\tif key, ok := residentGitKey(root, headBefore, args); ok {\n+\t\t\tmemoKey = key\n+\t\t\tif hit, found := memo.get(key); found {\n+\t\t\t\tif int64(len(hit)) > limit || !state.op.reserveInput(int64(len(hit))) {\n+\t\t\t\t\tstate.mu.Unlock()\n+\t\t\t\t\tstate.markUnknownForRoot(root, producer, \"Git command output exceeded the read-view input byte budget\")\n+\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n+\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\tstdout, memoized = hit, true\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif !memoized {\n+\t\tstdout, stderr, runErr = runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmittedContext(ctx, files, root, args, limit, state.op.reserveInput)\n+\t}\n \tif errors.Is(runErr, errGovernanceReadViewBudget) {\n \t\tstate.mu.Unlock()\n \t\tstate.markUnknownForRoot(root, producer, \"Git command output exceeded the read-view input byte budget\")\n@@ -348,9 +369,15 @@ func (state *governanceReadViewGitState) capture(files Files, ctx context.Contex\n \t\tswitch {\n \t\tcase byObject:\n \t\t\tobservation.pure = true\n+\t\tcase memoized && byHead:\n+\t\t\t// The commit is the one the memo's key names; nothing ran, so there is no second read.\n+\t\t\tobservation.pure, observation.headAt = true, headBefore\n \t\tcase byHead && headBefore != \"\" && governanceHeadAt(ctx, files, root) == headBefore:\n \t\t\tobservation.pure, observation.headAt = true, headBefore\n \t\t}\n+\t\tif memoKey != \"\" && !memoized && observation.pure {\n+\t\t\tmemo.put(memoKey, stdout)\n+\t\t}\n \t}\n \tstate.observations[key] = observation\n \tstate.mu.Unlock()","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"b6649492-0987-467e-a4e4-0feecd2bf9b4","timestamp":"2026-11-10T07:56:57.318Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex 007e8323..ba61c646 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -258,6 +258,7 @@ pose delegate handoff <run> --to <agent|auto> [--dry-run] [--json]\n pose delegate cancel <run> [--json]\n pose delegate agents [--json]\n pose runtime serve|start|attach|status|stop|restart [--idle <d>] [--drain <d>] [--json]  # optional per-worktree runtime; opt-in, standalone without it\n+pose runtime run [--envelope] [--timeout <d>] <review-check|closeout-check|artifact-check|surface-check|roadmap-check> [args...]  # runs the check in the runtime when there is one, else standalone\n \n # Project state and docs governance\n pose state [init|refresh [--if-stale]|diff]  # native project-state artifact; no subcommand = validate\n@@ -945,7 +946,7 @@ Reservations live in `.pose/review-attempts/`, final receipts link the run, and\n \n **Optional worktree runtime.** `pose runtime start` starts, detached, a runtime for this worktree; `attach` and `status` handshake with it, `stop` drains it (`--drain <d>`, default 5s) and says how many requests in flight finished and how many were abandoned, `restart` is stop then start, and `serve` runs it in the foreground (`--idle <d>`, default 30m, stops an idle runtime; 0 never does). It is opt-in: no other command starts it, and every command runs standalone whether it runs or not. The runtime is identified by the user, the canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) and the Git common directory, so two worktrees of one repository, or two users, never share one; the handshake compares the engine, build, protocol and schema as well and an attach from another engine is refused naming the field. Its endpoint is