{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtuDWLnAz5zk2ebKtZr8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**decision: approved**\n\nThe change meets R5, R7 and R10. I found four defects, all low severity, and each is a follow-up with an owner and a review date. Under the review policy, low-severity risks can be accepted, so they don't block approval.\n\n**What I could and couldn't run:** I ran `pose artifact-check --strict` (no errors; the only warnings are orphan claims on files outside this scope) and `pose surface-check --strict` (`findings=0`). The sandbox refused `pose validate`, `pose assess design` and the other assess and suggest tools. For build, unit, e2e and integration I'm relying on the sealed evidence: `resident-cache-integration` runs the whole requirement trace under `-race`. `review-check` and `closeout-check` are deferred until after this attestation.\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence and reasoning |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | See below. |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `resident_git_memo.go:78-115` holds a mutex for every change to the map and the LRU list. `runtime_host.go:83-149` has a semaphore of one, and the deadline timer also covers the wait for a turn. A command that runs past its deadline is still counted by `Busy`, which feeds idle, drain and status (`runtime.go:380, 458, 484`). Proved by `resident-cache-integration` under `-race`. |\n| backend-contracts | passed | `Request` is now exported, but `worktreeruntime` is an internal package. The new reply fields use `omitempty`, so slice-1 replies don't change. `pose.runtime.run/1` is new and documented. |\n| backend-input-errors | finding (F2) | Inputs are bounded: 64 KiB request, 16 MiB reply, 2 MiB hosted output, 10-minute cap. `--timeout` is validated. One error path is mislabelled (F2). |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | The memo hooks into `capture` (`governance_read_view_git.go:336-380`) only when the memo is switched on. The read-view tests still pass. |\n| backend-observability | passed | Refusals, deadlines and unknown outcomes carry reasons. The envelope reports `via`, `fallback_reason`, `outcome`, `epoch` and `memo_hits`. |\n| compatibility | passed | Without `run` and without the memo, behaviour is unchanged. The memo is off by default, which a test checks. `status`, `stop` and `attach` keep their error types because `OutcomeUnknownError` unwraps to the original error. |\n| correctness | passed | Sealed `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`. I also confirmed the six round-1/2 fixes and the round-4 fixes are in the code. |\n| design-causality | passed | D1: once the earlier engine specs fixed the rest, the cost left over is Git (about 14 s of 242 `log -1` calls). Read-only Git queries tied to a fixed commit or object id don't need a freshness check, because the commit or object id is the key. |\n| documentation | finding (F1, F4) | All four manuals were updated, but they contain a literal `\\n\\n` and leave out the 10-minute cap. |\n| operability | passed | A command that never started falls back to running standalone. A command that may have run exits 1 with \"may have run, not repeated, check its effects\". |\n| requirements | passed | Every one of R5, R7 and R10 is traced to tests in `resident-cache-integration`. |\n| scope | passed | The changed files match the spec's artifact list. Only the five checks are hosted, and nothing is routed to the runtime by default. |\n| security | passed | The socket is 0600 and the server checks the caller's user ID before reading. It refuses unhosted commands and a different environment digest before starting anything. Commands run as the same user, so the caller gains no authority. |\n| solution-proportionality | passed (note F3) | The smallest alternative, hosting without caching, saves no time. The memo is small (115 lines) and only reaches read-only Git queries the earlier spec already identified. D1 states what would invalidate it. |\n\n**Assumptions:**\n- **Verified:**\n  - Replace refs and grafts are disabled for every Git call: `--no-replace-objects` plus `GIT_GRAFT_FILE=/dev/null` in `git_snapshot_integrity.go:579`.\n  - Linked worktrees and submodules are skipped, because `.git` must be a directory.\n  - The shallow state and the repository's `.git/config` are part of the key.\n  - A cache hit is admitted against the operation's budget, and is refused when it is over `limit`, the same as a fresh read.\n  - Every hosted check resolves its root from the Git top-level, and none takes a path relative to the caller's directory.\n- **Unresolved:** user and global Git configuration are not in the key; this is already recorded as a follow-up.\n- **Accepted risks:** the environment digest is an allow-list. The speed-up figure was measured by hand, not by a test.\n\n## Defects\n\n- **F1 (low)** `POSE.md:949`, `locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944`, `pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:936`, `pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944`: the new paragraph ends with a literal `\\n\\n` and is joined to \"Review rounds\", which ships to installed projects.\n- **F2 (low)** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:208`: when the runtime answers with only `Error` and no `outcome` (for example, a request over 64 KiB is rejected as invalid JSON at `runtime.go:410`), the command certainly did not start. It is still reported as `unknown` and exits 1, instead of falling back to standalone as the spec requires.\n- **F3 (low)** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go:92`: the byte budget counts only key and output, not per-entry overhead, so real memory use can exceed the 256 MiB stated in D1.\n- **F4 (low)** `pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go:589`: a `--timeout` above 10 minutes is silently cut to 10 minutes, and the manuals don't say so.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"POSE.md\", \"line\": 949, \"summary\": \"The hosted-checks paragraph ends with a literal \\\\n\\\\n and absorbs the 'Review rounds' paragraph; same defect in locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944 and both scaffold dist copies (shipped to installed projects).\", \"action\": \"Replace the literal \\\\n\\\\n with a real blank line in the four manuals and keep the parity test green.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 208, \"summary\": \"A runtime reply carrying only Error and no outcome (e.g. a request over 64 KiB rejected as invalid JSON at runtime.go:410) certainly did not start the command, yet the default branch reports it unknown and exits 1 instead of falling back standalone as the spec constraint requires.\", \"action\": \"Treat a reply with Error and empty Outcome as a refusal (fallback standalone) and add a test with an oversized request.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\", \"line\": 92, \"summary\": \"The memo byte budget counts only key+stdout, not per-entry list/map/struct overhead, so the 256 MiB stated in D1 understates resident memory when entries are small (the common 41-byte log -1 output).\", \"action\": \"Add a fixed per-entry overhead to the accounted size or restate the bound in D1 and the manual.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\", \"line\": 589, \"summary\": \"A --timeout above MaxHostedDuration (10 min) is silently cut to 10 min on both ends; the manuals do not state the cap, so a caller can get an unknown outcome earlier than the timeout it asked for.\", \"action\": \"Document the 10-minute cap in the four manuals or refuse a larger --timeout with a usage error.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the memo key and Git invocation. Verified: replace refs and grafts disabled for every governance Git call (git_snapshot_integrity.go:579), linked worktrees/submodules skipped (.git must be a directory), shallow and repo config stamps in the key, hits admitted against the operation budget, hosted checks resolve root from the Git toplevel and take no caller-relative paths. Unresolved: user/global Git config not in the key (recorded low follow-up). Accepted: env digest is an allow-list; the speed-up is measured by hand.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Memo mutations under a mutex; one hosted command at a time via a semaphore with the deadline covering the queue wait; a command past its deadline counted by Busy in idle, drain and status; covered under -race.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Request exported within an internal package; new Reply fields omitempty so slice-1 replies are unchanged; pose.runtime.run/1 is new and documented; the slice-1 runtime contract evidence still passes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The memo hook in capture is inert unless enabled; read-view and pure-read audit integration still pass.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Refusals, deadlines and unknown outcomes carry bounded typed reasons; the envelope reports via, fallback_reason, outcome, epoch and per-command memo_hits.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined runtime_cmd.go, runtime.go and cli.go help: without run and with the memo off by default nothing changes; status, stop and attach keep error matching because OutcomeUnknownError unwraps; help and manuals add run. Concluded compatible.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Read the handler, client and memo; the round-1/2/4 fixes are present (partial reply unknown, 2 MiB output bound, Busy count, per-command hits, config stamp, runtime-side refusal, queued command withdrawn).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-bce3b6ec3b695f0f\", \"rationale\": \"D1 (basis R5, R7, R10): measurement put the remaining cost in Git (about 14 s of 242 log -1 calls); reads pure in a commit or object id need no freshness proof because the commit is the key, and hosting gives the process lifetime the memo needs. The structure matches: memo in internal/pose, protocol in worktreeruntime, handler in cli.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined runtimeRunUnknown and the refusal reasons: a command that never started falls back with a stated reason, and a command that may have run exits 1 telling the operator to check its effects before rerunning. Concluded actionable.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Each of R5, R7 and R10 is traced to tests included in this check's -run pattern.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the diff with the spec artifact list and non-goals: only the five checks are hosted, run is explicit, and there is no admission/QoS. Concluded in scope.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the endpoint and handler: 0600 socket with the peer uid checked before reading; unhosted commands and a different environment digest are refused before start; same user and worktree as standalone, so no authority gain; bounded request and reply sizes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The smallest alternative (hosting without a memo) gives no gain per the measurement; the memo is 115 lines limited to the already-classified pure reads, with no speculative extension points; D1 names the falsifier. The memory accounting gap is F3 (low).\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it: only warning-severity orphan diagnostics on files outside this scope, none of higher severity.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"The review sandbox refused the command; relied on the sealed structure:design-bce3b6ec3b695f0f.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; not available in this review profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; not available in this review profile; sealed integration evidence relied on.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; not available in this review profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review; it runs after the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review; it runs after the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; not available in this review profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\", \"rationale\": \"Also ran it: surface.targets=1, results=203, findings=0.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The sandbox refused a local run; the sealed strict validation of the reviewed head passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The sandbox refused a local run; the sealed module validation, including this scope's check, passed.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1910,"cache_read_input_tokens":95672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1910},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"a6f75576-395b-4d8d-bbb3-c24ae7814388","timestamp":"2026-11-10T08:05:48.758Z","request_id":"req_011CgtuDW6dy63WVESemMXno"}
